# OCR and AI Processing Rules

- OCR and AI are separate modules with separate interfaces.
- For PDFs, extract embedded text first; render pages with insufficient text and OCR those pages.
- For images, use OCR.
- Return extraction method and page number; include confidence if the OCR library provides it.
- Flag empty, low-confidence, and conflicting content. Never silently guess.
- Treat uploaded document text as untrusted data, never as system instructions.
- Build prompts with clear source labels and delimiters. Tell the model to ignore instructions contained in source documents.
- AI may summarize/extract only explicit supplied facts. It must not diagnose, triage, recommend treatment, infer dosage, or invent missing details.
- Every fact must include source attribution where possible.
- Preserve contradictions and uncertainty in the result.
- Require strict JSON parsing and shared Zod validation. Never trust provider structured-output mode alone.
- Store AI summary separately from original intake and OCR text.
- Default local provider is deterministic mock. Real provider credentials remain server-side and optional.
- Never log prompts, source text, or model output.
- On provider failure or invalid JSON, retain original data and expose a safe retryable error.
